      "message": "fix(motion): chamfer wall-law refusal names no part when the source is the stock\n\nThe #2435 refusal in ride_loops said a chamfer \"would ride into the part\"\nalso when the chamfer's source was the stock and no part was near (#2483,\na tilted stock-source chamfer). ride_loops does not know the source, so\nthe text now says \"would ride into the material under it\", which fits a\npart source and a stock source. No geometry or refusal condition changes.\n\nPinned by machining2d::chamfer_ride::tests::a_wall_farther_than_the_width_refuses_by_name.\n\nFixes #2521\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
